4.2 Stability Analysis of the Normalization Constant
The most significant result of this analysis is the demonstrated stability of the normalization constant 𝑲. The script automatically re-calculated 𝑲 using a subsample of the first 5 galaxies from the dataset and compared it to the value derived from the full 9-galaxy sample.
𝑲 for the full sample (N=9): 0.01175

